{"id":"da867c509aff7f4e","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-inner-measure.md","title":"Inner Measure","display":"df-inner-measure — Inner Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-inner-measure","aliases":["58-df-inner-measure","Inner Measure"],"display":"df-inner-measure — Inner Measure","depends_on":["[[58-df-measure-space]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-sigma-algebra]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-inner-measure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-inner-measure</span><span>Inner Measure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-inner-measure — Inner Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"58-df-sigma-algebra\">58-df-sigma-algebra</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\">\\((X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\)</span> (measure space)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_*:\\mathcal P(X)\\to[0,\\infty]\">\\(\\mu_*:\\mathcal P(X)\\to[0,\\infty]\\)</span> (inner-measure operator)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\)</span> (measure-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])\\)</span> (function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (inner-measure predicate)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>对非空 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C\\subseteq[0,\\infty]\">\\(C\\subseteq[0,\\infty]\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sup C\\coloneqq\\iota s\\;\\bigl(s\\in[0,\\infty]\\land(\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le s))\\land\\forall b\\in[0,\\infty]\\;((\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le b))\\to s\\le b)\\bigr)\">\\(\\sup C\\coloneqq\\iota s\\;\\bigl(s\\in[0,\\infty]\\land(\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le s))\\land\\forall b\\in[0,\\infty]\\;((\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le b))\\to s\\le b)\\bigr)\\)</span>。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}inner\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S(\\mu_*,\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])\\land\\forall A\\subseteq X\\;\\left(\\mu_*(A)=\\sup\\{\\mu(F):F\\in\\Sigma\\land F\\subseteq A\\}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}inner\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S(\\mu_*,\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])\\land\\forall A\\subseteq X\\;\\left(\\mu_*(A)=\\sup\\{\\mu(F):F\\in\\Sigma\\land F\\subseteq A\\}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Inner measure: approximation from inside by measurable sets; dual to outer</li>\n<li>Carathéodory measurability is a property of an outer measure and is not part of this inner-measure definition.</li>\n<li>Jordan: inner content from rectangles inside; pre-measure on algebra</li>\n<li>Regular measure: outer regular + inner regular approximation from both sides</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Halmos, Measure Theory</li>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-measure-space","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-sigma-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-sigma-algebra]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measure-space","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ (measure-space predicate, see [[58-df-measure-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])$ (function predicate, see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_*:\\mathcal P(X)\\to[0,\\infty]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"C\\subseteq[0,\\infty]","display":false},{"tex":"\\sup C\\coloneqq\\iota s\\;\\bigl(s\\in[0,\\infty]\\land(\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le s))\\land\\forall b\\in[0,\\infty]\\;((\\forall c\\in C\\;(c\\le b))\\to s\\le b)\\bigr)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}inner\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{InnerMeas}_S(\\mu_*,\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\mu_*,\\mathcal P(X),[0,\\infty])\\land\\forall A\\subseteq X\\;\\left(\\mu_*(A)=\\sup\\{\\mu(F):F\\in\\Sigma\\land F\\subseteq A\\}\\right)","display":true}],"bytes":1624,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-689","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-inner-measure.md|58-df-inner-measure]]（batch16）"}],"outgoing":["83a15c7e9b3817dc","36d7463d215be751","a740bdad87b97ac6"]}